==Battleground==
*4 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'Prude]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*2 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Darkmadillo]]s spawn after 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Shadow Boxer K]] spawns after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Le'Prude's appearance brings with it a bit of a tricky level. The problem here isn't the Sir Seals or Ginger Snaches, which are both relatively trivial support that mostly provide you with cash. Le'Prude isn't a massive problem either, as they can be pretty reliably stalled and chipped down with a combination of [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]], the latter of which is made even better by [[Cat Combo|Combo]] like [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] to boost its damage and health. If Roe gets off a weaken, you could even use a well-timed [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] to get a hit or two off, but otherwise Courier tends to get juggled.

The real challenge comes when the [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark enemies]] start spawning. The Shadow Boxer Ks will assist Le'Prude in pushing, and the Darkmadillos will make life tougher for anything trying to outrange Le'Prude (mostly [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]]. A [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] can work wonders against both (and is boosted by the same Combos as Manic Island!), but your best option may just be to lure and kill the Dark enemies before resuming the fight against Le'Prude. Hopefully, you'll be able to kill Le'Prude before this elephant pushes too far, but the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] Cannon can assist you with that. Once Le'Prude is dead, the stage has nothing left to pose a challenge.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Benefitting from the same Combos as Dark Lazer and Manic Island, it feels like Lunacia was made for this stage. Le'Prude's Freeze Immunity dulls her effectiveness a bit, but being Strong Against Red and Immune to Explosions makes her work quite well here. Just make sure to protect her well once the Dark enemies start coming.
*[[:Category:Cats with Explosion Immunity|Explosion-immune]] Ubers: A fairly short list at the moment, but anything with Explosion Immunity that can deal with Le'Prude's Omni Strike is good here. Especially notable are: [[Baki Hanma (Uber Rare Cat)|Baki Hanma CC]], [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|NEK-03 Cloud Emperor]], and [[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death's Daughter Lunacia]], all of whom reliably tank or outrange Le'Prude.

==Trivia==
*Synthol Swamp is named after a type of [[wikipedia:Site enhancement oil|site enhancement oil]], which unlike the previous two stages ([[The Bulking Grounds]] and [[Whey Wasteland]]), does not describe a muscle building technique, but rather a method of appearing that those techniques have been used. These oils are injected into the skin to alter the shape and size of the muscle, but obviously, this does not actually build muscle definition. The changes are only skin-deep, similarly to how [[Le'Prude]] was only visually changed by a recolor.

